-- doctest_marker.mdk — S2-2: doc's example detection must agree with
-- doctest.mdk's, so the italic "run by medaka test" marker cannot lie.
--
-- doctest classifies an input line by the literal 5-char `-- > ` prefix
-- (`isInputLine`, compiler/tools/doctest.mdk).  doc's segmenter keys on a `> `
-- prefix in the extracted comment BODY, and `commentBody`'s 2-char-strip
-- branch turns `--> x` into `> x` — a body doc used to fence and label as
-- verified while `medaka test` never ran it.

-- | A REAL doctest: the raw comment carries `-- > `, so `medaka test` runs it
--   and the fenced block below legitimately earns the marker.
--
-- > realExample 1
-- 2
export
realExample : Int -> Int
realExample x = x + 1

-- | NOT a doctest: the raw comment is `--> …` (no space after the `--`), which
--   `medaka test` never collects.  It must render as ordinary prose — no
--   marker, no fence — with the leading `>` escaped so Markdown shows the text
--   the author wrote instead of a blockquote.
--
--> fakeExample 1
export
fakeExample : Int -> Int
fakeExample x = x
